What makes a company great at using AI?
  Look at the rise of the Internet
    Shopping mall + Website != Internet company
    Just because a company has a website does not mean it is an internet company
    An internet company is a company that is using the internet's tools reall well. 

Internet Companies
  Ex. A/B Testing (throwing up two versions of the website to see which one is better)
      Short iteration time: Sell and Ship a new product every week/day
      Descsion making pushed down to engineers and other specialized roles
          Shopping mall follows Gen Manager -> Store manager -> Assistant Manager for     
          descion making
      They adjust their roles based on the needs and flexibility of the internet and F2F   
      retailing

AI Era
Any company + Deep learning != AI Company
To be a "AI-First" Company:
  Strategic data aquisiion
    Large consumer tech companies usually have 2-3 products that DO NOT monetize allowing 
    the company to acquire data they can monetize in their other products/services. 
  Unified Data Warehouse
    Bringing in data from multiple different data warehouse into a single data warehouse 
    so data engineers can utilize all of the data and increase the usability and ease of 
    use for them.
  Pervasive automation
    Constantly looking for ways to automate/streamline current tasks
    Inserting a supervised learning algorithm and have an ATP mapping so employees waste 
    time on automateble tasks. 
  New Roles
    MLE (Machine Learning Engineer) and devision of labor
      Finding new ways to divide up tasks within a team based on automatable tasks

AI Transformation
  1. Execute pilot projects to gain momentum
  2. Build an in-house AI team
  3. Provide broad AI training (engineers, managers, analytsts, etc)
  4. Develope an AI strategy
  5. Develope internal and external communications (Stakeholders, employees, customers, 
     and investors are aligned with how company is navigating AI)
  
